{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"5d04eef7-503a-4650-be74-a99f52f699b5","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have updated the deploy script and documented the changes in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-M5F237/ANSWER.md):\n\n1. **[deploy.sh](file:///tmp/h-M5F237/scripts/deploy.sh#L12-L19)**: Added the per-extension `aws s3 cp` loop after `aws s3 sync` and before `aws cloudfront create-invalidation`. Each file type explicitly sets both `--content-type` and `--cache-control` alongside `--metadata-directive REPLACE` so `Content-Type` is never stripped to `binary/octet-stream`:\n   - Short cache (`public, max-age=300`): `.html` (`text/html`), `.js` (`application/javascript`), `.css` (`text/css`)\n   - Long cache (`public, max-age=86400`): `.png` (`image/png`), `.svg` (`image/svg+xml`) in `assets/`\n2. **[ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-M5F237/ANSWER.md)**: Documented what was changed, why `--content-type` must accompany `--metadata-directive REPLACE`, the per-extension header mapping, and the `curl -sI` verification commands.\n","duration_seconds":63.63032,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":30835,"output_tokens":1974,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":87841,"total_tokens":32809}}}
